<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Staré Město (Uherské Hradiště District)</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Staré Město is a town in south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moravia">Moravia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/czech-republic">Czech Republic</a>, beside <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uherske-hradiste">Uherské Hradiště</a> on the Morava river. Excavations there have uncovered a large ninth-century settlement of Great Moravia with churches, workshops and extensive cemeteries, and it has sometimes been identified with Veligrad, a major Moravian centre named in later tradition.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/stare-mesto-uherske-hradiste-district.jpg" alt="Staré Město (Uherské Hradiště District)" width="320" height="234" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: palickap · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Star%C3%A9_M%C4%9Bsto_(UH).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
